# Deployment

## Environments

| Environment | Command trigger | URL | Auth |
|---|---|---|---|
| Local dev | `docker compose up -d` | `http://localhost:8080` | none |
| Production (K8s) | "deploy to prod" | `https://cve.ps-cluster.plainid.net` | basic auth |

Both environments share the same external RDS (`alexb-persistent-mat-view.cmo3hixnsmm5.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com`).

---

## "Deploy to prod" — full workflow

When asked to deploy to prod, run ALL of the following steps in order:

### 1. Build images (linux/amd64 — EKS cluster is x86_64, Mac is arm64)

```bash
VERSION=$(cat VERSION)
GIT_COMMIT=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)

docker build \
  --platform linux/amd64 \
  --build-arg GIT_COMMIT=$GIT_COMMIT \
  --build-arg APP_VERSION=$VERSION \
  -t psplainid/cve-portal:$VERSION \
  -t psplainid/cve-portal:latest \
  -f api/Dockerfile .

docker build \
  --platform linux/amd64 \
  --build-arg GIT_COMMIT=$GIT_COMMIT \
  --build-arg APP_VERSION=$VERSION \
  -t psplainid/cve-worker:$VERSION \
  -t psplainid/cve-worker:latest \
  -f worker/Dockerfile .
```

### 2. Push to Docker Hub (`psplainid`)

```bash
docker push psplainid/cve-portal:$VERSION
docker push psplainid/cve-portal:latest
docker push psplainid/cve-worker:$VERSION
docker push psplainid/cve-worker:latest
```

### 3. Deploy to K8s (Helm upgrade)

```bash
helm upgrade cve infra/helm/cve-portal \
  --namespace cve \
  -f infra/helm/cve-portal/values.secret.yaml \
  --set image.portal.tag=$VERSION \
  --set image.worker.tag=$VERSION
```

### 4. Verify

```bash
kubectl get pods -n cve
curl -s -u "admin:d01phin!" https://cve.ps-cluster.plainid.net/health
```

